<title>GERMANY: BHF-Bank 96 oper profit drops 5 pct.</title>
<headline>BHF-Bank 96 oper profit drops 5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996 (in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    358     vs 377</p>
<p>    Group net risk provisions		 185     vs 107</p>
<p>    Group own-account trading profit	73	vs 69</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 777     vs 748</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     461     vs 415</p>
<p>    Group business volume		     82,588  vs 73,523</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total		 74,144  vs 64,924</p>
<p>    Group equity ratio (BIS)		  9.4 pct vs 10.9 pct</p>
<p>    Number of staff			     3,050   vs 3,183</p>
<p>    DVFA earnings per share		   1.74    vs 2.05 dmk</p>
<p>    Dividend					1.45    vs 1.45 dmk</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is BHF-Bank AG. The bank said it had dissolved a small proportion of its hidden reserves to secure an unchanged dividend.</p>
<p>It also said its involvement with industrial holding company AGIV AG had shaved 109 million marks off its earnings in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
